{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/865973-mages-breaking-the-masquerade","id":865973,"title":"Mages Breaking the Masquerade","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-15T09:23:59-07:00","id":865973,"title":"Mages Breaking the Masquerade","content":"The Delirium takes care of itself as a natural phenomenon, but the Masquerade is carefully maintained by the Camarilla. Vampires have a lot more to lose than the other supernaturals if the secret gets out, there's no easy way to identify a Mage while Kindred just need to be exposed to sunlight.<br /> The Rule of Shade is enforced by the Traditions (and the Technocracy) but they have a lot less to fear from Hunters. Some enterprising Nephandi could cause a lot of havoc by publicly exposing the existence of the undead, making a lot of work for the 'good guys' so my question is why don't the bad guys throw a spanner in the works by ripping up the veil?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9496-barbelith","name":"Barbelith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9496_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T09:53:36-07:00","id":865986,"title":"","content":"Paradox for one.<br /> Technocracy.<br /> And besides, everyone knows how power hungry mages are, and how dangerous they are. i woudnt be surprised if someone took retilation against the subject in case he attempted something that stupid","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T12:01:36-07:00","id":866039,"title":"","content":"Besides just &quot;Paradox,&quot; the fact that doing magic obviously in front of Sleepers makes magic harder and Paradox worse is a big reason to keep to the shadows.<br /> <br /> Mages are also very squishy. For all of their mystical power, anybody with a gun can kill a mage who isn't prepared for an attack. And mages might not have a lot tells, but they have to work at being hidden to avoid those skilled in occult matters from noticing the tells they do have. Mages also don't have a lot of natural ways to tell if a non-mage is hunting them.<br /> <br /> Going public in the modern age is far more headache than it's worth. It basically means any reasonable mage is now going to have to start increasing the number of background protective spells that have up all the time up drastically to make sure some random religious fanatic Sleeper doesn't shank them for being a &quot;witch.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T14:23:19-07:00","id":866115,"title":"","content":"Mages work better in the shadows. One can better exploit the advantages that power has if said power it's unknown to your enemies, or to the people that you're going to manipulate.<br /> Besides, why molest Vampires, especially when you're a bad guy (and couldn't care less if people gets sucked)?. You can protect yourself better by hiding than by facing them.<br /> <br /> The Traditions plan to do this, eventually, but there's nothing to gain if people isn't willing to accept Magick (in the way that the Traditions define it).<br /> <br /> People forget Marauder attacks, and Nephandi work by subtly corrupting mages and other people. They gain nothing throwing that bone (or at least I don't see the advantage).<br /> <br /> The Taftani, however, had an agenda against subtle magick that included showing a lot of vulgarity, and then exploding because of Paradox. Lots of Taftani died because of that. However, the Masquerade didn't break, thus we have to accept that either the Technocracy can contain such an outburst, or that the Paradox erased or altered the memories of wittnesses (like in the Czar Vargo case), or both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-15-2016, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T07:16:47-07:00","id":866813,"title":"","content":"Technocrazy wouldn't allow to break masquerade, and World of Darkness isn't like our reality. There the people have readen some news about bloodsucker murders, but they don't believe like them by supernatural creatures, but mad serial killers with &quot;Renfield's syndrome&quot; or hematolagnia (blood fetishism). It's like if you see a TV inverview about a person who tells she has been healed by a Catholic saint's miracle or abducten by aliens. For lot of peopel the urban legend about vampires really is a &quot;failed conspirancy&quot; againts rational atheism for people to come back to religion. People knows there are serial killers who drinks blood, but they suposse they are only ordinary fool humans with false fangs. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T09:06:38-07:00","id":867601,"title":"","content":"There's no paradox involved.<br /> <br /> Let's say you are a Virtual Adept or New World Order Barrabi, a corrupted tech-savvy mage. You already have to spend a lot of effort hiding your nature from the Technocracy or Traditions so that's not really an issue. If you (for example) release some CCTV footage of kindred on Youtube &amp; Vimeo &amp; a slew of other public sites, that won't generate any Paradox because there's no magic involved. Showing some Sabbat feeding on a mortal would be an obvious choice, but really any clip showing supernatural stuff (or even just a gory murder) is going to attract a lot of attention.<br /> Unless you assume that some supernatural group has a lock on the entire internet, that genie is not going back in the bottle. You could argue that the Technocracy can scrub all instances of the video and mind-wipe anyone who spreads it, but realistically the Union does not have that kind of control (they wish they did). Even some theoretical alliance of Glass Walkers, Technocrats, Virtual Adepts and hacker Kindred allies is not going to be able to undo a leak like that- look at the Panama papers, the Snowden files, leaks are hard to mend.<br /> As a devious Nephandus wanting to keep the Technocracy busy, sending video clips of vampires doing their thing to a few hundred sleeper bloggers (through burner accounts &amp; seven proxies etc.) would be a great tactic to stir up a hornets nest of trouble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9496-barbelith","name":"Barbelith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9496_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T10:42:17-07:00","id":867655,"title":"","content":"Who needs to censor the Internet?<br /> <br /> People post videos of the &quot;supernatural,&quot; all the time on the real Internet... and nobody gives a shit. The vast majority of people assume it's either some freak camera error, or that its a hoax. There are TV shows dedicated to showing how such videos have rational explanations.<br /> <br /> If such a character is constantly posting really high quality vampire videos? They'll get a following of people that are enjoying it as entertainment because they appreciate the quality of such a hoax, a few nutjob followers, and maybe a couple takedown notices/get shutdown by the video sites after people complain about their likenesses being used without permission.<br /> <br /> The result of such things is pretty much going to be nil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T01:24:57-07:00","id":868265,"title":"","content":"Besides, unlike Vampire which is all about Masquerade... Mage is not about the same thing. Mage is all about changing perceptions and doing the impossible, hoping to awaken all of the world to the fact that they can do just what you can. So Masquerade is not really all that important in Mage, just as Mages are not all that important in Masquerade...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T09:49:48-07:00","id":868505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/865973-mages-breaking-the-masquerade?p=868265#post868265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides, unlike Vampire which is all about Masquerade... Mage is not about the same thing. Mage is all about changing perceptions and doing the impossible, hoping to awaken all of the world to the fact that they can do just what you can. So Masquerade is not really all that important in Mage, just as Mages are not all that important in Masquerade...</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed on the first, but I'm not so sure about the second. Sure, drinking blood, siring childer, using supernatural powers all have Masquerade implication, but Ascension, either individually or trying to &quot;uplift&quot; humanity (which covers the &quot;changing perceptions&quot; is a goal more like Golconda in Vampire (which doesn't really have any Masquerade implications, except possibly positive ones). Meaning, it is certainly out there and is definitely a possibility as a factor in a chronicle, but doesn't have to be and doesn't even seem to be based on the vast majority of examples of individual mages &amp; their goals and mage organizations &amp; what they actually do. <br /> <br /> I'd say the &quot;Masquerade&quot; in Mage is more intrinsic, in the problems casting anything resembling spells that affect the world (as opposed to, say, waving around a wand and saying made-up words while gas mains go up... since coincidental magic, by its very nature, has to have an apparent broken cause and effect relationship, even a broken proximate cause and effect relationship, really). If a vampire exploded like a full tick if someone caught her drinking blood, the Masquerade would track with Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T23:38:44-07:00","id":869138,"title":"","content":"Always remember that Dominate and Blood bind works on mages, even if they have Mind. Also, Tremeres have technomagic paths as well as spirit use paths. Presence also works over the Video monitor or internet. And a Manipulation 5 + Subterfuge 5 are not unknown in the oWoD. Anonymous is already the Camarillas Bitch. All this equals &quot; These are not the droids......I mean, There is no such thinks as Supernaturals out there. Must have been the 3 state blood drinker wanted by the FBI&quot; And if that guy didn't exist before, he sure would after!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11217-kurseteller","name":"kurseteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T00:39:57-07:00","id":869159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/865973-mages-breaking-the-masquerade?p=868505#post868505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed on the first, but I'm not so sure about the second. Sure, drinking blood, siring childer, using supernatural powers all have Masquerade implication, but Ascension, either individually or trying to &quot;uplift&quot; humanity (which covers the &quot;changing perceptions&quot; is a goal more like Golconda in Vampire (which doesn't really have any Masquerade implications, except possibly positive ones). Meaning, it is certainly out there and is definitely a possibility as a factor in a chronicle, but doesn't have to be and doesn't even seem to be based on the vast majority of examples of individual mages &amp; their goals and mage organizations &amp; what they actually do.<br /> <br /> I'd say the &quot;Masquerade&quot; in Mage is more intrinsic, in the problems casting anything resembling spells that affect the world (as opposed to, say, waving around a wand and saying made-up words while gas mains go up... since coincidental magic, by its very nature, has to have an apparent broken cause and effect relationship, even a broken proximate cause and effect relationship, really). If a vampire exploded like a full tick if someone caught her drinking blood, the Masquerade would track with Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm mostly pointing to the tone of the Average Mage game, which will involve utterly crazy shit that is bound to challenge the perception of the people around them and leave mayhem, legends and mystery in its wake. Sure, The Technocracy might clean it up, in their MiB manner but the world itself will seem crazier then the one in Masquerade. Mages want the people agitated and challenged, while Vampires want placid prey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T03:51:41-07:00","id":869211,"title":"","content":"The Traditions equivalent of the Masquerade is the Rule of Shade: &quot;Be subtle in your Arts, lest others know you for what you are.&quot;<br /> <i>'since the Burning Times, it\u2019s been common sense. Some folks obey this one more than others do, but given the prevalence of monitoring technology, video cameras, cell phones, and the dreaded YouTube post, a flashy wizard\u2019s basically writing her own death warrant.'</i><br /> <br /> But I was specifically talking about Mages exposing Vampires. I think Heavy Arms is probably right, getting people to believe it would be the problem- but look at the bigfoot photo, a convincing clip of supernatural activity would be quite likely to go viral and be widely shared, even as a novelty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9496,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9496-barbelith","user":"Barbelith","date":". 04-20-2016, 06:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9496-barbelith","name":"Barbelith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9496_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T08:05:34-07:00","id":869322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/865973-mages-breaking-the-masquerade?p=869159#post869159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm mostly pointing to the tone of the Average Mage game, which will involve utterly crazy shit that is bound to challenge the perception of the people around them and leave mayhem, legends and mystery in its wake. Sure, The Technocracy might clean it up, in their MiB manner but the world itself will seem crazier then the one in Masquerade. Mages want the people agitated and challenged, while Vampires want placid prey.</div> </div> </div> </div>In most of the Mage games I've played, the PC's don't actually actively want people agitated, it just seems to happen as they re-arrange the scenery in the process of doing magely things. In fact, in games where Paradox matters (and admittedly, it doesn't have to if the rules are run RAW with an open, as opposed to an even, hand), they are inspired to make things seem as &quot;normal if extreme&quot; as possible.<br /> <br /> Again, the assumption of wanting to &quot;challenge&quot; people by their actions is partially, but probably, rarely, true. As per the rules, it really doesn't have much of an effect to do vulgar magic in a spectacular but singular fashion, and, since mage is apparently supposed to be a traveling game, per Brucato when he stated that he would never foresee a &quot;place&quot; splat for the game, that's most people's interaction with mages. They blow into town, blow up town, blow out of town and might or not be followed by a NWO clean up squad.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean that the game can't be about trying to brainwash the hoi polloi, but, as I stated, though that game (like an &quot;Ascension&quot; game) is implied, it just doesn't seem to be the &quot;default&quot; game that gets described in the way the setting is set up, the way the NPCs act and their plans, etc. Notice that Mage the Ascension's opening fiction is about fighting the insidious Nephandi and it would be a chore to even torture it into something about Ascension. Calling the game &quot;Mage the Ascension&quot; was probably not a great idea. It would be like calling it &quot;Vampire the Golconda&quot; or &quot;Wraith the Transcendence&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T14:03:41-07:00","id":869633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/865973-mages-breaking-the-masquerade?p=869322#post869322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In most of the Mage games I've played, the PC's don't actually actively want people agitated, it just seems to happen as they re-arrange the scenery in the process of doing magely things. In fact, in games where Paradox matters (and admittedly, it doesn't have to if the rules are run RAW with an open, as opposed to an even, hand), they are inspired to make things seem as &quot;normal if extreme&quot; as possible.<br /> <br /> Again, the assumption of wanting to &quot;challenge&quot; people by their actions is partially, but probably, rarely, true. As per the rules, it really doesn't have much of an effect to do vulgar magic in a spectacular but singular fashion, and, since mage is apparently supposed to be a traveling game, per Brucato when he stated that he would never foresee a &quot;place&quot; splat for the game, that's most people's interaction with mages. They blow into town, blow up town, blow out of town and might or not be followed by a NWO clean up squad.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean that the game can't be about trying to brainwash the hoi polloi, but, as I stated, though that game (like an &quot;Ascension&quot; game) is implied, it just doesn't seem to be the &quot;default&quot; game that gets described in the way the setting is set up, the way the NPCs act and their plans, etc. Notice that Mage the Ascension's opening fiction is about fighting the insidious Nephandi and it would be a chore to even torture it into something about Ascension. Calling the game &quot;Mage the Ascension&quot; was probably not a great idea. It would be like calling it &quot;Vampire the Golconda&quot; or &quot;Wraith the Transcendence&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I do not necessarily mean that the mages blowing up shit, riding dragons and performing miracles are actually going into it for the Art and Transcendance. It's just that the consequences of their actions change the world. Like one of the characters who healed people in sight of others and became the saint, or another who changed the world of telecomunications and got a ton of cash through clever use of correspondance, or the people who still remember the fight between the Dragon and the giant robot atop the Golden Gate...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T05:19:08-07:00","id":870099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As a devious Nephandus wanting to keep the Technocracy busy, sending video clips of vampires doing their thing to a few hundred sleeper bloggers (through burner accounts &amp; seven proxies etc.) would be a great tactic to stir up a hornets nest of trouble. </div> </div> </div>Really?, because, to me, it seems like a great tactic to have Technocratic agents trying even harder to locate you (the technocracy allocates more resources when the threat it's higher, an it's bound that some, if not most, of those extra resources would be to silence the source) + having vampires trying to locate you. (In addition, you have curious Hunters on your track, and maybe a few others that were not even remotely aware of your existence until you turned youtuber).<br /> <br /> Nephandi want to infiltrate, they want to go unnoticed to spot the already existing corruption of Mages and work with it. You don't want to get attention, because that increases the risk of discovery and has no gain.<br /> Having both the Technocracy and the local Camarilla on your track doesn't seem like a good safety plan, unless you are working with others, and serving as a bait to cover THEIR actions.<br /> Even then, the result it's so unpredictable that doesn't seem like a solid plan, you have no business including the vampires in this, you can act as a bait without them.<br /> <br /> Besides, the Feed do have some spells that diminish the credibility of a video (in adition to the natural skepticism of people), thus merely posting on YouTube isn't going to be that transcendant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T09:29:36-07:00","id":870277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/865973-mages-breaking-the-masquerade?p=870099#post870099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides, the Feed do have some spells that diminish the credibility of a video (in adition to the natural skepticism of people), thus merely posting on YouTube isn't going to be that transcendant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spells?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I dearly hope you mean routine Procedures that simply take advantage of the fact that even a few hundred thousand youtube viewers seeing some fangs and blood and Twilight-like special effects (Celerity, Potence, Fortitude)...does not actually equal &quot;Masquarade is endangered.&quot;. Those youtubers or bloggers - majority of them young adults - will go to sleep; and back to work, university and friends &amp; families...and the idea of some Vampires hanging out there will drift away to being a rather amusing - if dark &amp; scary - urban legend inspired by mythology.<br /> <br /> For Masquarade endangering, you need to get onto the more respectable media, and this is extremely hard to do. The main two reasons would be the Camarilla and Technocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 04-22-2016, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T13:48:39-07:00","id":870583,"title":"","content":"Not only Technocrazy and vampires, also atheist sleeper humans who don't want society come back to religion. It would be the end of sexual revolution because people again feat God's judment in the afterlife. And another supernatural factions (for example Pentex) could suffer &quot;collateral damages&quot; if a &quot;vampire-slayer crusade&quot; starts. Some demons could help to the keep masquerade because they would rather people to be farest from the priests, without faith. The mafia would lose all amost their sinner clients, now reborn Christians. <br /> <br /> Really the mascarade is a broken like a open secret in the elite high spheres.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T14:03:32-07:00","id":870602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/865973-mages-breaking-the-masquerade?p=870583#post870583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not only Technocrazy and vampires, also atheist sleeper humans who don't want society come back to religion. It would be the end of sexual revolution because people again feat God's judment in the afterlife.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are religions/belief systems and codes of sexual conduct other than Christianity, you know. In fact, there are different interpretations of Christianity that probably wouldn't have a problem with greater sexual permissivity. Atheists aren't universally free-love types, and the two concepts have little to nothing to do with each other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And another supernatural factions (for example Pentex) could suffer &quot;collateral damages&quot; if a &quot;vampire-slayer crusade&quot; starts. Some demons could help to the keep masquerade because they would rather people to be farest from the priests, without faith. The mafia would lose all amost their sinner clients, now reborn Christians.<br /> <br /> Really the mascarade is a broken like a open secret in the elite high spheres. </div> </div> </div>Pentex could probably play that hysteria for a long while and to great profits It only has to sacrifice a few pawns to make it work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 04-21-2016, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T16:36:39-07:00","id":870750,"title":"","content":"And not all Mages give a damn about Religio.Those that do are as likely to believe and follow entities drastically different from the classic monotheistic Faiths. Judging all the Faiths by the benchmarks of Christianity is a fool's errand. Add to that do they would probably want to do some very nasty stuff to the Chorus for all the crap they put them through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T20:57:17-07:00","id":875223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbelith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/865973-mages-breaking-the-masquerade#post865973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Delirium takes care of itself as a natural phenomenon, but the Masquerade is carefully maintained by the Camarilla. Vampires have a lot more to lose than the other supernaturals if the secret gets out, there's no easy way to identify a Mage while Kindred just need to be exposed to sunlight.<br /> The Rule of Shade is enforced by the Traditions (and the Technocracy) but they have a lot less to fear from Hunters. Some enterprising Nephandi could cause a lot of havoc by publicly exposing the existence of the undead, making a lot of work for the 'good guys' so my question is why don't the bad guys throw a spanner in the works by ripping up the veil?</div> </div> </div> </div>That they could, but by definition, if one group gets exposed, the others could (and more likely would) be at risk of getting involved. And since mages have a lot of issues with Paradoxes creaping up on them, i am not sure that they would be 'safe'..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T09:18:41-07:00","id":875718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/865973-mages-breaking-the-masquerade?p=875223#post875223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That they could, but by definition, if one group gets exposed, the others could (and more likely would) be at risk of getting involved. And since mages have a lot of issues with Paradoxes creaping up on them, i am not sure that they would be 'safe'..</div> </div> </div> </div>But the Union has a huge edge in most of their activities being coincidental. In fact, using a lot of coincidental magic to keep and advance the coincidental nature of their magic. So they don't have nearly the incentive to keep it under wraps. Expose them and the NWO spin-doctors will make you look like a wacko conspiracy theorist. Or cast themselves as a secret organization of heroes who have been fighting the supernatural menace on the behalf of humanity all along, who are now relieved the secret is out and they can finally step out into the light of day and do their good and necessary work (and all those rumors about the shadier stuff... THAT'S the conspiracy stuff... Don't you know we're the heroes.... 'cause everyone else does...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T16:40:53-07:00","id":920627,"title":"","content":"As one Player put it.<br /> <br /> &quot;Vampire is about keeping the Masquerade, Mage is about breaking it.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampir